class_name SidePlans
extends RefCounted
## Floor plans of the side-view gang segments (M5): six per biome, each also mirrored (twelve), as
## ASCII like the room plans. Row 0 is the ceiling, row 10 the bottom; a column without ground in
## the bottom row is a pit. SideLayout parses and checks them (tests/unit/test_side_layout.gd and
## tools: scratchpad generator rules = SideLayout.check()).
##
## Legend:
##   #  rock (solid, rock_blob terrain)          =  ledge (one-way platform, front_* tiles)
##   H  ladder (top cell = a one-way step)       .  air
##   S  start (player feet on the cell bottom)   D  exit door
##   o  coin (run gold ×1.5)                     $  golden coin (1 soul crystal), the hardest spot
##   s  slime (hops)                             k  skeleton (walks)
##   ^  spike trap on the floor                  C  chest in a niche (optional)
##   t  wall torch                            T  turret mount (floor, ceiling or wall)
##   w  water / slime pool (slows running)
## Rules every plan follows (SideLayout.check): 40-60 columns, 11 rows, 8-14 platforms, 1-2 pits,
## a ladder or a change of level, 6-8 coins, one golden coin, 1-3 enemies, 1-3 spike traps, 1-2
## turret mounts away from start and door, at most one chest; start and door reachable, no dead end,
## every item in reach. Round 3 (16.10.2026): every plan got a turret mount (set up in
## SideRules.TURRET_CHANCE of the segments); per biome two new plans with a pool and spike runs:
## *_cistern-like (pool, pit, raised block, ladder up to the door) and *_ossuary-like (from high
## down past a spike wave under a ceiling turret, a pool, a ladder to a turret ledge, a crumbling or
## plain ledge over the second pit).

## Test aid (net_run_smoke side=1): every picked layout sets its turrets up (the draw still happens,
## so the RNG stream stays the same). Set on every machine before the run. Never in the game.
static var force_turrets_for_tests := false

